# Cloudflare Pages header rules.
#
# Cross-origin isolation is what makes SharedArrayBuffer available, which is what
# lets onnxruntime-web run multi-threaded WASM. Without these two headers the
# inference worker silently falls back to a single core and the latency budget
# work is wasted. This mirrors `crossOriginIsolationHeaders` in vite.config.ts,
# which covers dev and preview but not a deployed build.
#
# Cross-origin data (UCSC bigWig range reads, the UCSC sequence API) is fetched
# in CORS mode and UCSC sends `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`, so require-corp
# does not block it.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp

# Content-hashed by the bundler, so it can never go stale.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# The ORT WASM binary is 11.7 MB and versioned with the dependency, not the URL,
# so cache it hard but revalidate on deploy.
/ort/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
